# Paths marked export-ignore are omitted from `git archive`, which is how
# build-tarball.sh builds the customer deploy artefact. This is the ALLOWLIST
# side of the release boundary: git archive ships TRACKED files only, so
# untracked and ignored material (.hyperi-ai plans, .claude config, .ansible and
# .venv caches, a stray environments/<customer> inventory) can never reach a
# customer by accident. Only tracked-but-internal paths need naming here.
/build-tarball.sh export-ignore
/.github         export-ignore
/.gitattributes  export-ignore
/.gitignore      export-ignore
/test            export-ignore
